Playing in explore mode is fine in some ways, but it has some really
big disadvantages. If you make the wrong kinds of mistakes early in a
normal game, they will be fatal, and that's it.  In Explore mode, you
can come back to life and keep playing.  That's fine if it was a
stupid mistake that didn't really do much (e.g., you walked into a
floating eye; just don't do that again), but some mistakes stay with
you for the rest of the game if you do this.  For example. losing your
weapons and not getting a new one is rather fatal unless you're a
monk.  And it'll keep being fatal, because you haven't taken care of
the problem, and Explore mode can't solve that one!  Or if you get
poisoned down to very low strength, that's going to be fatal, and
Explore mode can't solve that problem, either - you'll keep dying
because the underlying fatal problem is still there.  So, if you keep
dying in Explore mode, figure something went wrong, your character is
really dead, and it's time to quit that game and start another one.

As has been suggested, playing the normal game is a rather good way to
learn from your mistakes, as long as you aren't attached to your
characters :)

